# Things left out of the image at build time (works like .gitignore, but for Docker).
# Background: ADD . /app in the Dockerfile puts the whole api-service folder into the image.
#             The files below are caches or system files made automatically when running locally. The image doesn't need them, so leaving them out keeps the image cleaner and the build faster.
# During development docker-compose mounts the code into the container. The mount is not affected by this file, only the built image is.

# Caches Python makes automatically at runtime
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Caches left behind by pytest and ruff
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Local virtual env (the image has its own /.venv, the one from the Mac can't be used)
.venv/

# Files the Mac makes automatically
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Safety net: if someone ever puts a key in this folder, it still won't be packed into the image
secrets/
*service-account*.json

# Keep local environment files out of ADD . /app.
.env*
